            <ArticleTitle>[The electronic patient record - a great opportunity to rethink medical information and its use].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2027-2030</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Since the early 2000s, the management of information concerning patient care has fundamentally changed. Previously stored in separate medical and nursing paper medical records, patient data are now gathered in a single electronic health record (EHR) thanks to the digitization of our hospitals, whose development and mastery are a major issue in today's health system.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
